The provider packs (packs/providers/) hold facts only: the names providers trade under, their AS numbers and the
addresses of their public pages. Each pack lists its sources, the date each was read and what its terms allow. No
text, logo or contact detail of any source is included. Some entries carry the id of the provider's Wikidata item
(https://www.wikidata.org/, CC0 1.0) as a cross-reference. Provider names are the trademarks of their owners and are
used only to identify them; this project is not affiliated with any of them.

The serial-number rules (packs/serials/) quote one sentence of each vendor's own public page as the ground of a
rule, with its address and the date it was read.

PyYAML (MIT licence) reads a definition of the device-type library when a model is imported.
